From 8d61b24d9a9516b39bae5f04bafaad90387d63b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:49:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(multiaxis): start and exit picks for the multi-axis
 contour

The Multi-Axis Contour (the drive-curve planner) takes a start point and
an exit point. Each pick acts on the drive curve nearest it. A closed
curve starts at its point nearest the start pick, and after its full lap
runs on to its point nearest the exit pick. An open curve starts and
leaves at the ends that the picks select.

Refused by name: a pick farther than 1.5 tool diameters from every
curve, an open curve's end too far from its pick, an exit at the start's
end, and a plunge or retract column at a picked point that crosses the
part. Without a pick the path is byte-identical.

The unit tests of curve.rs move to curve_tests.rs, unchanged.

Refs #3330

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
